  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "admin-note",
      "page": "admin",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Dark by default, like the console today. Desktop is the working surface; the phone artboard on the right is the same screen for approving a bill on the move."
    },
    {
      "id": "data-note",
      "page": "foundations",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "Properties, tenant names, slugs and the \u20b99/unit rate come from lib/config.js. Readings, amounts and contact names are sample data."
    },
    {
      "id": "open-pair",
      "page": "admin",
      "x": 1420,
      "y": 960,
      "w": 1000,
      "text": "Card open state \u2014 same tenant, web and mobile. Click a card to open it in place: check the photo, fix the reading, approve. Web spreads photo and entry side by side; mobile stacks them."
    },
    {
      "id": "tenant-default",
      "page": "tenant",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Tenant app \u2014 dark is the default (top row); the toggle in the header switches to light (row below). After submitting, three cards show: Total due, Meter reading (with the units chart in a collapsed \u201cView detailed units info\u201d accordion, shown open here), and Maintenance."
    },
    {
      "id": "cycle-note",
      "page": "cycle",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "What the tenant sees across one month, left to right: a new month opens with the reading due; after they submit, it locks and waits for the owner; once the owner finalises, the bill shows as Pending payment; when the owner marks it received, it reads Paid. These are the live app states (dark, the default) \u2014 the account and meter cards already render them from the owner's actions."
    },
    {
      "id": "movein-note",
      "page": "movein",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Move-in (new tenant): the owner adds the tenant and sends their link (Admin \u00b7 Add tenant), the tenant photographs the meter on move-in day and submits a starting reading (Tenant \u00b7 Welcome \u2192 Submitted), the owner verifies it against the photo (Admin \u00b7 Verify), and the tenant sees it confirmed \u2014 monthly billing begins on the 1st."
    },
    {
      "id": "moveout-note",
      "page": "moveout",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -160,
      "w": 1000,
      "text": "Move-out is TENANT-INITIATED. (1) The owner taps Start move-out on the tenant \u2014 no data entry. (2) The tenant's app unlocks a Final reading card; they photograph the meter on their last day and submit. (3) The owner gets a banner that the tenant wants to move out with the final reading. (4) One tap opens the settlement inside the console \u2014 same sign-in, prefilled with the final reading \u2014 where deposit, deductions and adjustments net to a refund or payable. (5-6) The tenant sees the settlement, then a clean Move-out complete once the owner deactivates the link."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "moveout"
  }
}